   6: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   7:     """
   8:     Stamp the input sprite in a periodic right-and-down pattern where every third horizontal copy is pink.
   9: 
  10:     Input structure
  11:     - A black/dominant background contains exactly one 8-connected foreground sprite.
  12:     - The sprite has a tight bounding box; its mask, height, and width define the repeated tile.
  13:     - Repeated copies are separated by one background row or column.
  14: 
  15:     Rule
  16:     - Starting at the sprite's original upper-left bbox corner, place slots every sprite_width+1 columns.
  17:     - On the original sprite row, fill the horizontal slots with the sprite mask; slots 0,1,3,4,... keep the source color, while slots 2,5,8,... become pink.
  18:     - Starting at each pink horizontal slot, repeat pink copies downward every sprite_height+1 rows.
  19:     - Clip any copy that extends beyond the grid edge.
  20: 
  21:     Key insight
  22:     - The first row establishes a repeating two-source-color then one-pink rhythm, and only the pink columns continue vertically.
